# Track B — CONTROL PIN: `String s = g.get(); d.put("k", s)` — the NAMED-LOCAL
# form of the sibling temp cell.
#
# This is the exit-0 CONTROL that discriminates the temp path from the
# named-local path. `ensure_owned_at_boundary` (context.rs:2516) unconditionally
# applied the borrow-detection predicate to var-decl RHS since forever, so this
# named-local form has been correct all along. The temp form failed only
# because `ensure_owned_at_consuming_arg`'s else arm dropped the predicate.
#
# Green BEFORE Track B's fix (var-decl clone path) and BOTH AFTER — the fix
# unifies the two consumer paths on this predicate.
#
# HEAP-FORCED VALUE (never a literal — a rodata String has cap=0, so a false
# negative would look like the bug is absent).

String heaped():
    return "hello " + "world" + "-forced"

void main():
    Mutex[String] m = Mutex[String](heaped())
    Guard[String] g = m.lock()
    Dict[String, String] d = {}
    String s = g.get()
    d.put("k", s)
    print(d.len())
